# BAD2: --vmem-controller s28 needs --virtual-memories
# Page columns (state paged to HBM, --storage <class>:pages=hbm; S28 A2): a column's read and write of one host cycle
# may be of two instances (the adapter carries both); K instances share an HBM row, lane = inst mod K (K the most
# whole-byte lanes in a 512-bit beat, at most the instances), each write masked to its lane. Driver/Inputs/paged:
# 128-bit page words (K 4), 64-bit columns (K 4, three columns on one local switch with the RAM), 32-bit columns with
# bubbles (K 16). Exact; the table's E_LANES, the rows' instances / K. Mutant: the adapter's lanes 2 for 4 (lane =
# inst mod 2): a lane's write lands on another instance's bytes and the run mismatches.
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/paged && foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/pg2 --static --page 2 --storage Leaf:pages=hbm --virtual-memories Leaf:ram --vmem-controller s28 Leaf > %t/pg2.log 2>&1
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/paged && foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/pgc --static --page 1 --page-hbm-column-bits 64 --storage Leaf:pages=hbm --virtual-memories Leaf:ram --vmem-controller s28 Leaf > %t/pgc.log 2>&1
