# MUT: {{^}}MISMATCH
# Rows of 17 bits (2^17-row RAMs; A2's fixed row field had 12): the words' instance and row fields are the design's
# widest memory's (INST_W 1, ROW_W 17: a 609-bit request, a 527-bit response), parameters of every unit and the
# kernel's (foldsim_sim.vh). Exact against the target; a model that keeps 12 row bits aliases rows and mismatches; units
# built at ROW_W 12 refuse the 17-bit memory.
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/vmem17 && foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/w17 --static --virtual-memories ram --vmem-controller s28 --ready-ahead --room-ahead Leaf > %t/w17.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=W17 < %t/w17/foldsim_sim.vh
# W17: `define FOLDSIM_S28_INST_W 1
# W17-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_S28_ROW_W 17
# W17-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_S28_MEM_W 4
# W17-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_S28_REQ_W 609
# W17-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_S28_RSP_W 527
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=W17SV < %t/w17/foldsim_sim.sv
# W17SV-DAG: output {{ *}}[608:0] s28r0_0_req_word,
# W17SV-DAG: input {{ *}}[526:0] s28r0_0_rsp_word,
# W17SV: foldsim_vmem_adapter #(
# W17SV-NEXT: .IW(1),
# W17SV-NEXT: .AW(17),
